The creator dashboard data is already live at `GET /stats/creator` (trend gaps, idea pipeline, competitors) — same queries as your Obsidian Home dashboard, now over SQL.

## Run order

```bash
docker compose up -d db
cp .env.example .env                 # point VAULT_PATH at your CortexVault
cd backend && pip install -r requirements.txt && cd ..
make migrate && make sync            # expect: scanned ~17, edges ~30 on the seeded vault
make api                             # :8000  → /docs for interactive API
cd web && npm install && cd ..
make web                             # :3000  → search "second brain", click nodes
make smoke
```

**Honest caveats:** (1) `EMBED_PROVIDER=hash` makes everything run offline, but vector ranking is meaningless until you set `openai` + your key — then `drop table chunks;`, re-migrate, re-sync (keyword + graph results are real even in hash mode). (2) Changing `EMBED_DIM` requires the same chunks rebuild. (3) The sandbox verified parser/sync/retrieval logic against an in-memory connection; the SQL itself is written for pg16 + pgvector and needs your Docker run to confirm end-to-end.

Next slice when you're ready: **Research Agent** — RSS/arXiv/competitor-upload cron that drops items into `Inbox/`, invokes the headless Librarian, and lets the sync engine ripple it into the graph automatically.